{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And I will settle.</b> Doubled [forms] of the hif'il, like <i>and I will cut off</i> (Leviticus 26:22), from the root of <i>the king's rage subsided</i> (Esther 7:10). The meaning of <b>and I will settle</b> is in the manner of people finding rest, and the tribe of Levi among the twelve, and behold Joseph is in one staff."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Resolved the parenthetical (טמאתך) as a verse citation, Leviticus 26:22; it appears corrupted in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:12.233763436Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}